      "side": 1,
      "message": "For followup CL:\n\n----\n\n**2. Variable Shadowing in `fp_command_frame_v0** In the modified `fp_command_frame_v0` function, you declare `enum ec_error_list ret;` at the top of the function. Inside the `if (idx \u003d\u003d FP_FRAME_INDEX_RAW_IMAGE)` block, you redeclare it with a different type:\n\n```c\n\tif (idx \u003d\u003d FP_FRAME_INDEX_RAW_IMAGE) {\n\t\t/* The host requested a frame. */\n\t\tenum ec_status ret \u003d get_frame(offset, size, (uint8_t *)out);\n\t\tif (ret !\u003d EC_RES_SUCCESS) {\n\t\t\treturn ret;\n\t\t}\n\n```\n\nWhile this compiles, variable shadowing is a known code smell that can lead to confusion and bugs during future refactoring.\n\n* **Remediation:** Rename the inner variable to reflect its specific type (e.g., `status`), or remove the type declaration if you intend to reuse an appropriately scoped variable.\n\n```c\n\t\tenum ec_status status \u003d get_frame(offset, size, (uint8_t *)out);\n\t\tif (status !\u003d EC_RES_SUCCESS) {\n\t\t\treturn status;\n\t\t}\n\n```",
